## HOLDS (standing lines; binding)
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** before each C-entry, row, comment and ticket: `git log -S'<symbol>' --oneline` on the records worktree; `/usr/bin/grep -i -n` over the three files, `Registers/` and the catch-up folder; Jira `text ~` with controls. **A STATUS without a `PRIOR WORK` section naming, per item, what you searched and found is returned unread.**
2. **STATUS is the only channel.** No mail, chat, PR comment, issue comment, publish or upload; no message to any human. Ticket comments are the only client-visible words and address no person. Nothing is sent to HP.
3. **No production, no deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any app host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker.** Network: Jira (HPSMPOC) and `gh api -X GET` under the project's `GH_CONFIG_DIR`; `git push` of `records/b756` only. Code repo: READ verbs only (**no `workflow_dispatch`, no PR action, no re-run of any check, no branch-protection write**). **CodeQL is never bypassed and no alert is dismissed.** `decision_queue.sh` is never run.
4. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `git checkout --` on a tracked file); quarantine to `.tools/b756/_quarantine/`. A wrong Jira comment gets a correcting comment; a wrong ticket gets a comment, never an edit.
5. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`; heredocs QUOTED; zsh does not split an unquoted `$VAR` and expands a word starting with `=`: use `bash` script files for loops. **Every count printed in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it.**
6. **Locks, by path.** `.tools/b756/lock.sh` wraps git REF WRITES ONLY. No heavy job exists in this brief (no npm, no dotnet, no test, no workflow run).
